.nh
.TH "PB-RECIPE-ROTATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recipe-rotate - Give a recipe a new token; its machines keep working


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recipe rotate <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Give a recipe a new token. The old token stops working at once; machines already
paired from it keep running. Without --confirm, print what changes and the
confirmation code; run it again with --confirm <code>\&. The new token is printed once:
replace PB_RECIPE everywhere the old one is stored.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	the confirmation code printed without --confirm

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rotate

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON (the new token included, once)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recipe rotate ci
  pb recipe rotate ci --confirm K3M9QX
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recipe(1)\fP
